-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner relations for the Čerednik level groups
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a_1,b_1$, a non-zero squarefree natural number $N$, and primes $q,q'$ with $q'\neq q$, $q,q'\ge 5$ and $q,q'\nmid N$; fix further primes $r,\bar r$ with $\bar r\neq r$ and $r,\bar r\nmid N$. Assume $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly for the place $v$ containing $\bar r$. Let $\Lambda_1$ be a maximal $\mathbb Z$-order, $R_1\le\Lambda_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$ in the first), and $n_1$ a finite-adelic unit in $\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}\,R_1\,r$, i.e. $n_1$ and $r\,n_1^{-1}$ lie in the adelic box of $R_1$ while $n_1^{-1}$ and $r^{-1}n_1$ do not; write $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,\beta=R_1\cap\beta R_1\beta^{-1}$. Let $v_2$ be the place containing $r$. For each prime $\ell\notin\{q,q'\}$ let $s_2(\ell)\in\mathbb H^\times$ and $sf_2(\ell)$ a finite-adelic unit whose component at every place not containing $r$ is $s_2(\ell)\otimes 1$ and whose component at places containing $r$ is $1$, such that $\ell\cdot sf_2(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}\,\Lambda_1\,(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1)\,\ell$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in $\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}\,(\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1)\,\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_2(\ell))=\ell$. Let the base group $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$ consist of those $x\in\mathbb H^\times$ lying, at every place $w\neq v_2$, in the subgroup generated by the local unit box of $R_1$, and with $\mathrm{ord}_r\,\mathrm{nrd}(x)$ even, and let $\Gamma_2(\ell)=\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})\cap s_2(\ell)\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})s_2(\ell)^{-1}$. Let $w_2,\bar w_2$ assign to each index $j$ (i.e. $\mathrm{none}$ or a prime $\ell\notin\{q,q'\}$) elements of $\mathbb H^\times$ such that: $w_2(j)$ is a local unit at all places $\neq v_2$ of $R_1$ for $j=\mathrm{none}$, resp. of $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,(sf_2(\ell))$ for $j=\ell$, with $\mathrm{nrd}(w_2(j))=r$; and $\mathrm{nrd}(\bar w_2(j))=\bar r$, with $\bar w_2(j)$ a local unit of the same order at every place $u\neq v_2$ not containing $\bar r$, and with conjugation by $\bar w_2(j)$ preserving the local box of that order and the local box of $\Lambda_1$ at every place $u\neq v_2$. Then for every index $j$: $w_2(j)\Gamma_2(j)w_2(j)^{-1}=\Gamma_2(j)$, $\bar w_2(j)\Gamma_2(j)\bar w_2(j)^{-1}=\Gamma_2(j)$, $w_2(j)^2\in\Gamma_2(j)$, the commutator $w_2(j)\bar w_2(j)w_2(j)^{-1}\bar w_2(j)^{-1}\in\Gamma_2(j)$, and $\bar r^{-1}\bar w_2(j)^2\in\Gamma_2(j)$ (the scalar taken through the diagonal embedding); moreover, for every prime $\ell\notin\{q,q'\}$ the four elements $w_2(\ell)w_2(\mathrm{none})^{-1}$, $s_2(\ell)^{-1}w_2(\ell)s_2(\ell)w_2(\mathrm{none})^{-1}$, $\bar w_2(\ell)\bar w_2(\mathrm{none})^{-1}$ and $s_2(\ell)^{-1}\bar w_2(\ell)s_2(\ell)\bar w_2(\mathrm{none})^{-1}$ lie in $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$.
--
--   These are the Atkin–Lehner relations for the cocompact arithmetic groups that uniformise the Shimura curves of level $N$ and $N\ell$ in the Čerednik–Drinfeld $p$-adic uniformisation: the elements $w_2$ of reduced norm $r$ and $\bar w_2$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalise each level group, square into it up to the scalar $\bar r$, commute modulo it, and are compatible with both degeneracy maps of the level-raising tower. The statement is used in establishing that the Atkin–Lehner involutions on the Mumford-curve models are involutive, commute, and are Galois-equivariant, and in the construction of the descent intertwining data.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraph_atkinLehner_relations_levelGroups_place.lean

